  <title>Duplicate contact finder</title>

  <p><guiseq><gui>Administration</gui><gui>Duplicate contact
  finder</gui></guiseq> lists contacts that share a name, address, phone or
  other field, and merges duplicates.</p>

  <steps>
    <item><p>Under <gui>Column to sort</gui>, select the field to look for
    duplicates in, such as the phone number. Every contact sharing that field
    with another is listed, sorted by it.</p></item>
    <item><p>Type into the <gui>Filter text</gui> beside a field to narrow the
    list down.</p></item>
    <item><p>Select the contacts that are the same (hold <key>Ctrl</key>) and
    click <gui>Continue</gui>.</p></item>
    <item><p>Select the contact the others will be merged into, and click
    <gui>Merge</gui>. <gui>Cancel</gui> goes back.</p></item>
  </steps>

  <p>Merging moves every invoice, payment, purchase order, job sheet, file
  and other record of the other contacts onto the one you kept, then deletes
  the others. It cannot be undone.</p>

</page>
